  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday through next Friday)\nIssued at 1155 PM CDT Fri Oct 23 2026\n\nMonday the weather system will still be present across the\nsouthern plains only now departing to the east. This will keep the\nfetch of moisture across the eastern panhandles. Further rain\nshowers and thunderstorms have a medium chance of developing\nwithin this moisture for Monday. This will allow for additional\nrain accumulations in the eastern panhandles. There remains a low\nchance for flooding as the moisture will still be climatologically\nhigh. However, since there is lesser potential for training of \nstorms this threat will most likely be less compared to Saturday \nor Sunday. The weather system will in large depart come Monday \nnight with the rain showers and thunderstorms coming to an end. \nFor Tuesday the flow will shift to a broad southwesterly which \nwill promote drier conditions over the panhandles that persist \nthrough Wednesday. Come Thursday through Saturday the pattern \ncontinues to adjust over the southern panhandles. This will allow \nfor another fetch of moisture to move into the southern \npanhandles. The can bring another period of wet weather for the \nend of the week into the weekend.",
